            "review_text": "Kenny W\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam6 contributions\n0\nAuthentic-tasting Korean food, US-sized portions\nSep 2015\nBe warned, this place can get rather hot. Not because of the gochu jang (pepper paste) or Korean girl clientele, but due to the location of the restaurant - which is at the back of Kumho on the 1st floor. Large fans are used to try to cool the sauna-like conditions down, but given the sticker prices and prestigious address, aircon really should be used by the owners.\n\ntry any of the soups or stews (jiggaes) which are quite authentic tasting. Also, try the King-Sized Kim Bap - they're a meal for two!\n\nThis restaurant is a welcome change of pace to their Korean restaurant neighbors, with a relaxed, casual \"drinking\" establishment atmosphere. \n\nBe sure to bring plenty of mates, as the portions are fairly big (think US-sized).\nRead more\nWritten December 15, 2015",
