            "review_text": "LaneOne\nOttawa, Canada149 contributions\n0\nGreat Classic Korean Lunch Spot.\nJun 2015 • Friends\nHaving lived in Korea for almost four year, am always on the look-out for high-quality, fresh Korean cuisine around the world. This place is fantastic. Located on the 1st floor of the KumHo Asiana Plaza (where many Korean business are Headquartered in Vietnam, Jeon Sool Bap is the one of the best Korean restaurants I have visited outside of Korea, of course. Note, however, that this is not a Korean BBQ restaurant, but more aligned, as the name implies, to rice dishes and jeon (Korean pancakes). Have visited the restaurant once a week since I discovered it a month or so ago. One of five Korean restaurants in this complex, and by far the best. Prices are very reasonable (similar to prices in Seoul for similar fare). Side dishes are great. Service is excellent. It does get fairly busy if you don't get there before 12:15. Am told it is also quite busy after work when it attracts the Korean after-work drinking crowd.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 18, 2015",
